            "review_title": "Review at Ngon Ngon Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Harry B\nWellington, New Zealand1 contribution\n0\nExpensive food from a misleading menu\nFeb 2016 • Couples\nThe restaurant building is clean, spacious and has a nice view. This, however, applies to the other places in the Lotte building as well.\n\nThe food is expensive. You can get similar food at any other restaurant in Hanoi, or even on the street.\n\nThe menu's English is very misleading, and the staff will do nothing to correct it. I was disappointed to discover that the 'fried beef with salad' was actually deep fried, and that the 'salad' was actually just a handful of shrimp crackers. The staff simply shrugged and said that the crackers were a salad.\n\nBest to avoid. There are better restaurants in the Lotte centre, and better Vietnamese restaurants in Hanoi.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2016",
